{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["# Heteroscedastic BNN: Aleatoric/Epistemic Uncertainty + CVaR + Chance Constraints\n","\n","This notebook models a common industrial situation: not only the conditional mean, but also the **variance changes with the operating condition**.\n","\n","```text\n","heteroscedastic data\n","      ↓\n","BNN learns μ_w(x) and σ_w(x)\n","      ↓\n","Var(Y|x,D) = E_w[σ_w²(x)] + Var_w[μ_w(x)]\n","      ↓\n","posterior predictive scenarios\n","      ↓\n","chance-constrained and CVaR decisions\n","```\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["import random, numpy as np, pandas as pd, matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","import torch, torch.nn as nn, torch.nn.functional as F, pyro\n","import pyro.distributions as dist\n","from pyro.infer import SVI, Trace_ELBO, Predictive\n","from pyro.infer.autoguide import AutoDiagonalNormal\n","from pyro.nn import PyroModule, PyroSample\n","import pyomo.environ as pyo\n","SEED=42\n","random.seed(SEED); np.random.seed(SEED); torch.manual_seed(SEED); pyro.set_rng_seed(SEED)\n","torch.set_default_dtype(torch.float32)\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 1. Synthetic heteroscedastic demand\n","\n","Promotions, weekends, and extreme temperatures increase both expected demand and volatility.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["n=320; day=np.arange(n)\n","promo=np.random.binomial(1,.25,n); weekend=((day%7)>=5).astype(float)\n","temp=22+9*np.sin(2*np.pi*day/90)+np.random.normal(0,2.2,n); season=np.sin(2*np.pi*day/30); trend=day/(n-1)\n","true_mu=105+17*promo+9*weekend+13*season+.45*temp+8*trend\n","true_sigma=4+5.5*promo+3*weekend+.22*np.abs(temp-22)\n","demand=true_mu+np.random.normal(0,true_sigma)\n","Xr=np.column_stack([promo,weekend,temp,season,trend]).astype(np.float32); yr=demand.astype(np.float32)\n","Xm,Xs=Xr.mean(0,keepdims=True),Xr.std(0,keepdims=True)+1e-6; ym,ys=float(yr.mean()),float(yr.std()+1e-6)\n","X=torch.tensor((Xr-Xm)/Xs); y=torch.tensor((yr-ym)/ys)\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 2. BNN with mean and scale heads\n","\n","The observation model is\n","\n","\\[Y|x,w \\sim N(\\mu_w(x),\\sigma_w^2(x)).\n","\n","`softplus` keeps the scale positive.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["class HeteroBNN(PyroModule):\n","    def __init__(self,d,h=20):\n","        super().__init__(); self.h=PyroModule[nn.Linear](d,h); self.mean=PyroModule[nn.Linear](h,1); self.scale=PyroModule[nn.Linear](h,1)\n","        self.h.weight=PyroSample(dist.Normal(0,.8).expand([h,d]).to_event(2)); self.h.bias=PyroSample(dist.Normal(0,.8).expand([h]).to_event(1))\n","        self.mean.weight=PyroSample(dist.Normal(0,.8).expand([1,h]).to_event(2)); self.mean.bias=PyroSample(dist.Normal(0,.8).expand([1]).to_event(1))\n","        self.scale.weight=PyroSample(dist.Normal(0,.5).expand([1,h]).to_event(2)); self.scale.bias=PyroSample(dist.Normal(-1,.5).expand([1]).to_event(1))\n","    def forward(self,x,y=None):\n","        h=torch.tanh(self.h(x)); mu=self.mean(h).squeeze(-1); sigma=.03+F.softplus(self.scale(h).squeeze(-1))\n","        pyro.deterministic('mu',mu); pyro.deterministic('sigma_x',sigma)\n","        with pyro.plate('data',x.shape[0]): pyro.sample('obs',dist.Normal(mu,sigma),obs=y)\n","        return mu\n","\n","pyro.clear_param_store(); model=HeteroBNN(X.shape[1]); guide=AutoDiagonalNormal(model)\n","svi=SVI(model,guide,pyro.optim.Adam({'lr':.01}),loss=Trace_ELBO()); losses=[]\n","for step in range(3200): losses.append(svi.step(X,y)/len(y))\n","plt.figure(figsize=(8,3)); plt.plot(losses); plt.xlabel('SVI step'); plt.ylabel('ELBO / observation'); plt.show()\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 3. Law-of-total-variance decomposition\n","\n","For posterior samples \(w_s\):\n","\n","\\[\\widehat V_{alea}=S^{-1}\\sum_s \\sigma_{w_s}^2(x),\\qquad \\widehat V_{epi}=Var_s(\\mu_{w_s}(x)).\n","\n","The reported aleatoric term is the posterior expectation of conditional observation variance.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["def posterior_at(raw_x,S=3000):\n","    x=torch.tensor((np.asarray(raw_x,dtype=np.float32).reshape(1,-1)-Xm)/Xs)\n","    out=Predictive(model,guide=guide,num_samples=S,return_sites=('obs','mu','sigma_x'))(x)\n","    obs=out['obs'].detach().numpy().reshape(-1)*ys+ym; mu=out['mu'].detach().numpy().reshape(-1)*ys+ym; sig=out['sigma_x'].detach().numpy().reshape(-1)*ys\n","    return obs,mu,sig\n","\n","def decompose(obs,mu,sig):\n","    va=float(np.mean(sig**2)); ve=float(np.var(mu,ddof=1))\n","    return {'aleatoric_sd':np.sqrt(va),'epistemic_sd':np.sqrt(ve),'total_sd':np.sqrt(va+ve),'empirical_predictive_sd':np.std(obs,ddof=1)}\n","\n","low=posterior_at([0,0,22,.2,1.02]); high=posterior_at([1,1,34,.2,1.02])\n","pd.DataFrame([decompose(*low),decompose(*high)],index=['lower-noise condition','higher-noise condition']).round(3)\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 4. Risk-aware capacity decisions\n","\n","Use the high-volatility posterior predictive distribution as uncertain demand.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["samples=high[0]; rng=np.random.default_rng(SEED); S=500; d=rng.choice(samples,S,replace=False)\n","# Empirical 95% service-level decision\n","x_chance=float(np.quantile(d,.95))\n","# CVaR decision via grid search for clarity\n","c,h,p,alpha=1.0,.30,5.0,.95\n","grid=np.linspace(np.quantile(d,.2),np.quantile(d,.995),300)\n","def loss(x,D): return c*x+h*np.maximum(x-D,0)+p*np.maximum(D-x,0)\n","def cvar(L):\n","    q=np.quantile(L,alpha); return L[L>=q].mean()\n","scores=np.array([cvar(loss(x,d)) for x in grid]); x_cvar=float(grid[np.argmin(scores)])\n","print('Empirical 95% chance decision:',round(x_chance,2)); print('CVaR95 decision:',round(x_cvar,2))\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 5. Why mean-only uncertainty is dangerous\n","\n","If observation noise is ignored and only posterior mean-function samples are used, the upper demand tail can be severely understated in volatile operating regions.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["mean_only=high[1]; print('95% quantile, full predictive:',round(float(np.quantile(samples,.95)),2)); print('95% quantile, mean-function only:',round(float(np.quantile(mean_only,.95)),2))\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Takeaway\n","\n","Risk-sensitive optimization should use the relevant predictive distribution, not only epistemic uncertainty or only a point forecast. Heteroscedastic modeling is particularly important when process variability changes with the decision or operating state.\n"]}],"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","language":"python","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.x"}},"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":5}